------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-06-22] PHASE 2 -- characterize the offset pattern | OK
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The offsets are NOT consistent and NOT a cascade. They are single-digit OCR
substitutions in the FILED number, decomposed digit-by-digit:

  22 of 24 high/med candidates differ from the filed number by exactly ONE digit.
  Dominant confusion pairs (filed_digit -> audit-heading_digit):
     5 -> 0 : 8 cases   (units place -> +/-5 ; tens place -> +/-50)
     3 -> 8 : 6 cases
     8 -> 3 : 2 cases
     5 -> 9 : 2 cases
     others (5->3, 4->3, 3->2, 7->1, dropped digit) : 1 each
  The "+/-5 and +/-50" the audit flagged are simply a 5<->0 misread in the units
  vs the tens column. The "+/-50" is NOT a 50-chapter sequence shift.

Sequence-integrity check of the FILED chapter_int (the decisive test):
  1913: 636 acts, range 1..699, ZERO duplicate chapter_int, only 63 sparse gaps
        (genuine missing chapters); page order monotonic except 3 steps, all of
        which are the flagged candidates themselves (heading-OCR noise, not a
        real reorder).
  1917: 773 acts, range 1..803, ZERO duplicate chapter_int, 30 sparse gaps,
        page order PERFECTLY monotonic (0 inversions).
  => The filed chapter_int forms a clean, monotonic, dup-free 1..N spine in both
     volumes. A "+/-50 cascade" would have produced a block of duplicate/colliding
     chapter_int values; there are none. This alone rules out a sequence bug.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-06-22] PHASE 3 -- ground-truth via LOCAL header-OCR | OK
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE on the arbiter: in these volumes the page-TOP running head is the PRINTED
PAGE NUMBER + "FORTIETH SESSION." / "STATUTES OF CALIFORNIA." -- NOT "CHAPTER N".
"CHAPTER N" appears only as the body act-heading. Pages routinely carry 2-3 acts.
So the arbiter used was: (a) the full-page multi-psm header scan (all CHAPTER-N
headers on the page, deduped) and (b) confirmation that filed N sits between
confirmed neighbors N-1 and N+1 on the adjacent pages.

Full-page header scan result (filed number found on its own page):
  1913: 12/16 FILED-CONFIRMED directly; 4 residuals resolved by neighbor check.
  1917:  6/8  FILED-CONFIRMED directly; 2 residuals resolved by neighbor check.

Sample ground-truth (which number is correct -- ALL came out FILED-correct):
  1913 ch35  p95  : page header scan = [35]               -> FILED 35 (audit 30 = 5->0)
  1913 ch56  p115 : = [56,57]                             -> FILED 56 (audit 36 = 5->3)
  1913 ch65  p128 : = [65,66]                             -> FILED 65 (audit 60 = 5->0)
  1913 ch130 p275 : =[180,131]; ch129 confirmed p274      -> FILED 130 (audit 180 = 3->8)
  1913 ch168 p307 : =[163]; ch169 confirmed p309          -> FILED 168 (audit 163 = 8->3)
  1913 ch318 p666 : =[]; ch317@p663 & ch319@p671 confirmed-> FILED 318 (audit 313 = 8->3)
  1913 ch455 p942 : =[455]                                -> FILED 455 (audit 405 = 5->0)
  1913 ch566 p1012: =[566]                                -> FILED 566 (audit 966 = 5->9)
  1917 ch43  p39  : =[42,48]; ch42 & ch44@p40 confirmed   -> FILED 43 (audit 48 = 3->8)
  1917 ch155 p240 : =[155,156]                            -> FILED 155 (audit 150 = 5->0)
  1917 ch259 p448 : =[259,260,261]                        -> FILED 259 (audit 299 = 5->9)
  1917 ch354 p487 : =[354,355,356]                        -> FILED 354 (audit 304 = 5->0)
  1917 ch605 p933 : =[605]                                -> FILED 605 (audit 600 = 5->0)
  1917 ch773 p1619: =[1773("773"+pgno1)]; ch772 & ch774 confirmed -> FILED 773 (audit 173 = 7->1)

  Result: in EVERY high/med case the FILED chapter_int is correct; the audit's
